Author:     yjyang62 <yangjinyang5@huawei.com>
AuthorDate: Fri Oct 23 18:00:18 2026 +0800
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 23 18:00:18 2026 +0800

    [CI][PCP] Migrate weekly DSA-CP cases to PCP (#19643)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Migrate 29 Weekly configurations from DSA-CP to PCP. Each former DSA-CP
    TP group becomes TP1 with the same PCP size (4, 8, or 16), preserving DP
    and device counts. The 19 PD cases use MooncakeConnectorV2, including
    MultiConnector children, with matching P/D metadata and unchanged decode
    topology.
    
    Adjust HCCL buffers from existing MC2 logs and TP1 capacity
    calculations. Keep model features, workloads, benchmark baselines, and
    thresholds unchanged. A5 retains its existing EPLB configuration and
    scheduling; support for its legacy SwiftBalance settings remains
    separate work.
    
    The change set is carried over unchanged from #19435 (same 29 files,
    same diff); no additional edits were made on top of it.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Weekly test configurations only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed all 29 configurations and rendered 316 PD service commands;
    checked device allocation, TP/PCP mapping, embedded JSON, P/D metadata,
    and unchanged benchmark definitions.
    - Existing test configurations were migrated; no new test implementation
    was added.
    - NPU/model tests were not run. Startup, memory use, accuracy, and
    performance validation remain pending.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Where applicable, unit tests
    cover boundary conditions.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: Where applicable, a regression test covers
    the bug.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: Abnormal execution paths are
    covered.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: Hardware benchmark results and performance
    regression coverage are attached.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: leolee <yihao.li@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: leolee <yihao.li@huawei.com>

